# GGMI Mexico: Reallocating Media Weight, with a Post-FOMC Reassessment

**Entity:** GGMI, GAIN Global Markets Inc. (Mexico, forex.com/es)
**Prepared for:** FOREX.com
**Prepared by:** brlvnt
**Date:** August 27, 2026
**Measured against:** Approved August 2026 monthly budget by channel (FOREX.com tracker, last updated 08/06/2026)
**Status:** DRAFT for FOREX.com review. Not for distribution.

---

## 1. Executive recommendation

The August budget is being spent almost in full. What is wrong is where it goes.

Bing produces a submitted application for $379 and is running at 62% of its approved budget. Azerion produces one for $978, has become more expensive every month since April, and is running at 123% of its approved budget. Native produces none and is running at 115%. The program is not overspending. It is funding its weakest channel and starving its strongest.

brlvnt recommends the **Controlled Pullback: $62,446 a month, a 50% reduction against the approved $125,000.** It funds Bing to the full $30,000 already approved for it, halves Azerion, holds a reduced and monitored Quantcast line, and removes Native. A **Deep Pullback at $30,000** is presented as the alternative if cash preservation outweighs everything else.

The reduction should be temporary and time-bound to a date rather than to a product launch. We recommend reassessing after the September 15 to 16 FOMC meeting.

