**The budget is being spent.** Delivery is within $3,442 of the approved figure across the four live channels. This is not a pacing problem, and the reduction below is not proposed to fix one.

**The allocation is inverted.** The channel with the lowest cost per submitted application is the only one materially under its budget. The two channels running over their budgets are the most expensive one and the one with no attributed applications at all.

**That is the whole argument.** Every recommendation in this document follows from moving weight from the second group to the first.

